# nsMsgProgress::UnregisterListener behavior in mailnews/base/src/nsMsgProgress.cpp

Gets the supplied object's weak reference, fails if unavailable, then removes the first matching entry. Returns failure if absent. Header equality compares weak-reference object identity, not listener behavior or names.

## State read

- listener; mListenerInfoList

## State changed

- Removes matching ListenerInfo

## Calls and triggers

- Dialog unload calls unregister at156; native compose STOP handler unregisters at3362; successful retry unregisters MessageSend at411.
- Firefox nsAutoTObserverArray::RemoveElement at218-226 adjusts active iterator positions after removal.

## Result and consumers

NS_OK only when matching entry removed; no-op absence is NS_ERROR_FAILURE.

## Errors

Unavailable weak reference -> NS_ERROR_INVALID_ARG; missing registration -> NS_ERROR_FAILURE.

## Async completion

Synchronous, safe iterator-position adjustment matters when called from callback.

## Ownership and cleanup

Drops array's weak-reference entry; does not destroy a strongly owned listener.

